# Rust build output.
/target
**/target

# The workspace Cargo.lock IS committed, deliberately: see docs/dependencies.md. Builds pass
# --locked so a dependency is never picked up silently. Only the backup file is ignored.
Cargo.lock.bak

# fuzz/ is the exception. It is a development tool outside the workspace, nobody installs it,
# and its dependencies reach no published artifact — so letting them float keeps it working
# as libfuzzer tracks nightly, rather than freezing it against a compiler that has moved on.
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Node. This project has no npm dependencies; node_modules only ever appears because a
# script installed Ajv transiently, and package-lock.json is that install's leftover.
node_modules/
/package-lock.json
packages/npm/*.tgz

# The WebAssembly module, built by `just wasm` from crates/onyx-wasm. Never committed:
# a binary in the tree is a thing nobody can review.
packages/npm/pkg/
*.wasm

# Python. examples/reader-py is run directly and caches bytecode beside itself.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Merge and patch leftovers, which are easy to commit by accident.
*.orig
*.rej

# Editors and operating systems.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

